{offset205}{arialbld}Tyron Spirex{arial}

Aircraft carrier the "Vandaume"{offset0}







Welcome to {arialbld}Sokumi{arial} {rank}.

I don't know if you've accepted this mission out of exoticism or simply the excitement of fighting at my side, but in any case you should know that this mission will be nothing like a cruise and more like a one-way ticket to hell.{pause}

Clarissa Jackson, the president of the Federation of Schyzo States, kindly invited me for tea. She has insisted that this affair be concluded promptly so that our men can return home for Christmas. Thus the name of this operation will be: {arialbld}TSUNAMI{arial}. The Tsunami, {name}, is the Nikonese name given to huge tidal waves caused by underwater earthquakes, very frequent in this region.{pause}


fig-1










{center}{device26}












{pause}The TSUNAMI strategy hinges on sea and air, each of our aircraft carriers (fig-1) can hold up to eight Kormoran fighters (fig-2). With this naval deployment, we possess an aerial support unit force for all amphibious operations on the Nikon archipelago.{pause}


fig-2










{center}{device31}












{pause}Our first customer's name is {arialbld}Padir Natkrof{arial}, he's presently sojourning at {arialbld}Bikin.{arial}


{ia3}{offset100}Natkrof is the admiral of the Katzar fleet, a Zirgol of course. The Zirgol clan inhabits the oriental steppes of Katzarin all the way to the Sea of Karal. No Zirgol has ever challenged the Katzar-Khat, but they are savvy politicians who've kept the upper hand on the admiralty for seven generations. 
By popular use, "The Zirgol" has become the title for Admiral of the Katzar Fleet. Izmir Natkrof, Padir's uncle, was the Zirgol for the Khat Piotr Margarin and his grandfather, Kotmir Natkrof, that of the terrible Khat Yozef Starin.{offset0}{pause}


Like all Zirgols, Natkrof is a skilled liar, he can offer an alliance if things aren't going his way and attack us as soon as we turn around. 


{offset150}{arialbld}Tyron Spirex{arial}

Commander of Operation TSUNAMI




